From f3ef3a72cf121813cd9db45b31e345ef974349c4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lovelace's Square <noreply@lovelacesquare.org>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 09:53:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] Let assistants connect: a setting that opens every
 window's control channel

A window opened from the file manager has no control port, so an
assistant the user works with (an MCP client, say) cannot join the
window the user is editing. File > Options > Agents gets "Let assistants
connect to this window", off by default. When on, a window started
without --control opens its control channel as `--control auto` does
(a free port, the key file named after it); the key is still required
on every request.

- ui-egui: UiState::allow_assistants (allowAssistants in ui.json, off
  when missing or junk), the `ui.allowAssistants` command (works without
  a document, like the other settings), the checkbox and a note in
  File > Options > Agents (not on the web, which has no control
  channel), and WordApp::set_control for a channel opened while the app
  runs.
- wordcraft: the setting picks `auto` at start-up when no port was given;
  changed while running, it is saved at once (so windows opened next
  follow it) and turning it on opens this window's channel. Turning it
  off leaves an open channel until the window closes. A channel opened
  only for this keeps the Start screen.
- docs: control-protocol.md lists ui.allowAssistants.

